#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:149
msgid "4.2 Attribute Inheritance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:150
msgid ""
"When you digitize a new interpretation polygon, SecInterp attempts to "
"automatically inherit attributes from underlying data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:151
msgid ""
"**Geology Overlap**: If the new polygon overlaps with a projected "
"geological outcrop, it will pre-fill the name and units."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:152
msgid ""
"**Drillhole Proximity**: If the polygon starts or ends near a drillhole "
"interval, it will inherit the lithology/rock unit from that interval "
"(e.g., \"Andesite\", \"Tuff\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:153
msgid ""
"**Manual override**: You can always manualy change the inherited color or"
" name in the properties dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:155
msgid "4.3 Exporting to 3D (PolygonZ)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:156
msgid ""
"SecInterp now bridges the gap between 2D sections and 3D modeling. This "
"feature allows you to export your 2D interpretations as real 3D objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:158
msgid "**Workflow:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:159
msgid ""
"Go to the **Advanced** tab in the **Settings** tab and check **\"Enable "
"3D Interpretation Export\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:160
msgid "Use the **Save** button (not Export) to generate your data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:161
msgid "The plugin will create a **PolygonZ** Shapefile in your output folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:162
msgid ""
"Every vertex of your interpretation is projected into real-world 3D "
"coordinates based on the section plane and surface elevation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:163
msgid "**Note**: This feature is now standard and available to all users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:165
msgid "4.3 Settings Page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:166
msgid ""
"The **Settings** page manages export configurations and advanced "
"features. It is organized into three sub-tabs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:168
msgid "1. Default Tab (Export Selection)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:169
msgid "Control exactly what gets generated when you click **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:170
msgid "**Topographic Profile**: Exports the surface line (CSV/SHP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:171
msgid "**Geological Profile**: Exports projected contacts (CSV/SHP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:172
msgid "**Structural Data**: Exports projected structural measurements (CSV/SHP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:173
msgid ""
"**Drillhole Data**: Exports traces (`LineStringZ`) and interval cylinders"
" (`PolygonZ`) as 3D Shapefiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:174
msgid "**Interpretations (2D)**: Exports your drawn polygons (SHP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:176
msgid ""
"![Default settings showing Export "
"Selection](images/guide_settings_default.png) *Default settings showing "
"Export Selection.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:176
msgid "Default settings showing Export Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:179
msgid "2. Advanced Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:180
msgid ""
"**Enable 3D Interpretation Export**: Toggles the generation of "
"**PolygonZ** Shapefiles for your interpretations. This creates true 3D "
"geometries based on the section plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:182
msgid ""
"![Advanced settings with 3D Export "
"feature](images/guide_settings_advanced.png) *Advanced settings with 3D "
"Export feature.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:182
msgid "Advanced settings with 3D Export feature"
msgstr ""

