msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:191
msgid "5. Preview Panel & Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:192
msgid ""
"The right-hand panel acts as an interactive canvas for your cross-"
"section. It includes a toolbar and specific controls to manage "
"visualization and performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:194
msgid "5.1 Toolbar Buttons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:195
msgid "Located at the top of the preview panel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:197
msgid ""
"**Preview**: Triggers a refresh of the rendering based on the current "
"configuration in the Settings/Data tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:198
msgid ""
"**Measure**: Activates the interactive ruler. Click on the canvas to "
"measure distances and gradients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:199
msgid ""
"**Interpret**: Activates the digitization tool for drawing geological "
"polygons completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:200
msgid ""
"**Export (Image)**: Saves the **current view** as an image file (PNG, "
"JPG, PDF, SVG). *Note: To export SHP/CSV data, use the main SAVE button.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:202
msgid "5.2 Visualization Controls (LOD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:203
msgid "These settings optimize performance for high-resolution datasets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:205
msgid ""
"**Max Points**: Manually limits the number of vertices rendered for "
"profile lines. Lower values improve zoom/pan speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:206
msgid ""
"**Auto**: When checked, the plugin automatically calculates the optimal "
"`Max Points` based on your current window size and resolution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:207
msgid ""
"**Adaptive**: Enables intelligent sampling algorithm. It preserves key "
"details in complex areas (steep topography, folds) while simplifying flat"
" or linear sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:209
msgid "5.3 Layer Visibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:210
msgid ""
"Use the `Show **` checkboxes to toggle specific data layers on or off "
"without reloading data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:212
msgid "**Show Topography**: The topographic profile line derived from the DEM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:213
msgid "**Show Geology**: Projected geological contacts from surface mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:214
msgid ""
"**Show Structures**: Structural measurements (dip/strike) projected onto "
"the plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:215
msgid "**Show Drillholes**: Borehole traces and geological interval cylinders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:216
msgid "**Show Interpretations**: Polygons and units digitized by the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:218
msgid "5.4 Using the Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:220
msgid "Measure Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:221
msgid ""
"**Snap-to-Vertex**: Measurements automatically anchor to real data points"
" (DEM or Drillholes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:222
msgid "**Multi-Segment**: Click multiple times to measure a polyline path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:223
msgid ""
"**Result Panel**: Displays Total Distance (3D), Horizontal Distance, and "
"Vertical Delta."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:225
msgid ""
"![Measuring distance along a drillhole "
"trace](images/guide_measure_tool.png) *Figure 7: Measuring distance along"
" a drillhole trace.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:225
msgid "Measuring distance along a drillhole trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:228
msgid "Interpretation Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:229
msgid "**Draw**: Left-click to add vertices for a new geological unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:230
msgid ""
"**Edit**: Vertices snap to existing lines to ensure topological "
"consistency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:231
msgid ""
"**Finish**: Double-click to close the polygon and assign attributes "
"(Lithology, Formation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:233
msgid "6. Closing & Saving"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:235
msgid "It is important to understand the difference between **Save** and **OK**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:237
msgid "**\"Save\" Button (Export to Disk)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:238
msgid "Use this when you want to **share** your data or use it in other software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/USER_GUIDE.md:239
msgid ""
"Generates physical files (Shapefiles, CSV) in your select **Output "
"Folder**."
